WEBVTT

00:00:18.352 --> 00:00:21.939
Kozakura sure didn't waste any time.

00:00:21.939 --> 00:00:24.149
Yeah, she ate an awful lot.

00:00:24.149 --> 00:00:28.362
This turned out to be one expensive apology.

00:00:30.155 --> 00:00:32.241
Toriko! You're not done yet?

00:00:32.241 --> 00:00:34.826
The "Make It Up to Kozakura" meeting is over.

00:00:34.826 --> 00:00:38.330
It's time for the
"Sorawo and Toriko Make Up" party!

00:00:38.330 --> 00:00:41.124
M-Make up?

00:00:41.124 --> 00:00:42.501
Excuse me!

00:00:42.501 --> 00:00:44.753
Be right there!

00:00:44.753 --> 00:00:49.299
We'll have edamame, potato salad,
tomato salad, the assorted skewers,

00:00:49.299 --> 00:00:53.387
chicken <i>karaage</i>, horse meat tartare,
seaweed and jako fish <i>daikon </i>salad, and

00:00:53.387 --> 00:00:57.683
seared vinegared mackerel, and...
Sorawo? You're not ordering anything?

00:00:59.643 --> 00:01:01.728
Okay, let's go with that for now.

00:01:01.728 --> 00:01:05.023
You got it. I'll clear away these empty plates.

00:01:05.023 --> 00:01:07.150
Thank you.

00:01:09.319 --> 00:01:13.156
Do you really plan on finishing all that?

00:01:13.156 --> 00:01:16.952
It'll work out as long as there's the two of us.

00:01:32.968 --> 00:01:37.514
<i>School never taught me what friends are</i>

00:01:37.514 --> 00:01:42.895
<i>People are such difficult creatures</i>

00:01:42.895 --> 00:01:47.316
<i>This world where you never</i>
<i>know what's said behind your back</i>

00:01:47.316 --> 00:01:52.863
<i>Looks a little ugly to me</i>

00:01:52.863 --> 00:01:57.743
<i>Compassion and ego sway on the scales</i>

00:01:57.743 --> 00:02:02.289
<i>They've swayed ever since I met you</i>

00:02:02.289 --> 00:02:05.209
<i>Your trespassing did a number on me</i>

00:02:05.209 --> 00:02:09.505
<i>It's not like anyone would do</i>

00:02:09.505 --> 00:02:10.672
"Kisaragi"
"Katasu - Yami"
<i>Is your empathy and complicity just an act?</i>

00:02:10.672 --> 00:02:15.010
<i>Is your empathy and complicity just an act?</i>

00:02:15.010 --> 00:02:19.348
<i>Like a fish out of water</i>

00:02:19.348 --> 00:02:21.642
<i>Delicacy and literacy</i>

00:02:21.642 --> 00:02:24.228
<i>Might not be necessary</i>

00:02:24.228 --> 00:02:27.314
<i>I just want to be wanted</i>

00:02:27.314 --> 00:02:29.816
<i>Selfish little me</i>

00:02:29.816 --> 00:02:33.987
<i>The scales have tipped</i>

00:02:33.987 --> 00:02:36.240
<i>As friends</i>

00:02:36.240 --> 00:02:42.246
<i>Let's meet in a secret place</i>

00:03:03.100 --> 00:03:06.895
There you are. Please enjoy.

00:03:06.895 --> 00:03:08.897
Thanks.

00:03:15.445 --> 00:03:17.447
Oh, I almost forgot. Look.

00:03:17.447 --> 00:03:20.784
The hat we found when we
returned from the Otherside?

00:03:20.784 --> 00:03:23.829
You said it looked weird.

00:03:23.829 --> 00:03:28.417
Yeah, it had a faint silver glow, but...

00:03:28.417 --> 00:03:30.085
Hmmm...

00:03:30.085 --> 00:03:31.295
Do you want it?

00:03:31.295 --> 00:03:32.880
No, I don't, I don't.

00:03:32.880 --> 00:03:35.424
Then do you mind if I keep it?

00:03:35.424 --> 00:03:39.344
I don't know how you can put
that creepy thing on your head.

00:03:39.344 --> 00:03:41.597
How's it look?

00:03:41.597 --> 00:03:43.974
You know you look good no matter what you wear.

00:03:43.974 --> 00:03:46.226
What? Really?

00:03:46.226 --> 00:03:49.062
Enough already. Take off
the hat while you're eating.

00:03:49.062 --> 00:03:50.772
Fine.

00:03:57.112 --> 00:03:59.031
So, when can you go again?

00:03:59.031 --> 00:04:00.949
Again?

00:04:02.367 --> 00:04:07.122
But... aren't you scared?

00:04:07.122 --> 00:04:12.753
Last time, we both nearly ended up dead.

00:04:12.753 --> 00:04:15.047
Yeah, but we didn't.

00:04:15.047 --> 00:04:16.840
You're not scared?

00:04:17.799 --> 00:04:21.512
Sure, I'm scared. But that's okay.

00:04:21.512 --> 00:04:24.181
I would've given up long ago if I was alone,

00:04:24.181 --> 00:04:26.183
or maybe even died before that.

00:04:26.183 --> 00:04:31.438
See? I knew you were scared.
So how can you want to go again?

00:04:31.438 --> 00:04:35.317
Well, it always works out as
long as we have each other!

00:04:35.317 --> 00:04:36.735
Huh?

00:04:38.153 --> 00:04:40.572
Is that really the issue?

00:04:44.826 --> 00:04:46.995
Did you miss me?

00:04:46.995 --> 00:04:49.831
Oh, what could this be?

00:04:49.831 --> 00:04:54.878
It must be the check. How much was it, Sorawo?

00:04:54.878 --> 00:04:56.880
Nineteen thousand and eight yen.

00:04:56.880 --> 00:04:58.841
Nineteen thousand and...

00:04:58.841 --> 00:05:02.719
Huh?! We really <i>did </i>go overboard.

00:05:02.719 --> 00:05:05.347
A lot of it's Kozakura's.

00:05:05.347 --> 00:05:07.891
Let's have them put it on a separate check.

00:05:07.891 --> 00:05:12.145
Is that really possible? But more importantly...

00:05:12.145 --> 00:05:15.107
Are you all right? Can you make it home alone?

00:05:15.107 --> 00:05:17.526
Probably, maybe!

00:05:17.526 --> 00:05:23.282
If I could handle marine basic training,
and I'm not saying I could...

00:05:23.282 --> 00:05:25.576
What are you talking about?

00:05:26.618 --> 00:05:29.371
Um, hi.

00:05:29.371 --> 00:05:35.544
I was wondering if we could have
a separate check for our friend who left.

00:05:35.544 --> 00:05:39.173
Since there is sublance,
the abardmont will be coming.

00:05:39.173 --> 00:05:41.466
Huh?

00:05:41.466 --> 00:05:45.470
The abardmont's coming, so...

00:05:45.470 --> 00:05:47.931
Huh?!

00:05:47.931 --> 00:05:50.350
Did you understand what he said?

00:05:50.350 --> 00:05:54.062
Hmm? I wasn't listening.

00:05:55.063 --> 00:05:56.356
Thank you.

00:05:56.356 --> 00:05:59.401
Thank you!

00:06:10.621 --> 00:06:14.041
Hey, let's go.

00:06:14.041 --> 00:06:15.792
Okay.

00:06:23.634 --> 00:06:26.386
Did you just bark?

00:06:26.386 --> 00:06:27.846
Hmmm?

00:06:27.846 --> 00:06:30.599
Never mind.

00:06:30.599 --> 00:06:33.602
Sorawo, which way's the station?

00:06:33.602 --> 00:06:36.647
It's that way, you dummy.

00:06:37.689 --> 00:06:40.692
Isn't it kinda dark?

00:06:40.692 --> 00:06:43.237
Maybe they're conserving electricity.

00:06:43.237 --> 00:06:47.533
They didn't have to
make it this dark. Am I right?

00:06:59.503 --> 00:07:02.589
I don't remember the station being this far.

00:07:02.589 --> 00:07:04.174
Hm?

00:07:48.719 --> 00:07:52.472
Ah, Sorawo, you went the wrong way.

00:07:53.515 --> 00:07:56.310
You're pinning the blame on me?

00:07:56.310 --> 00:08:00.731
Wait a second. Did Ikebukuro
always look like it's in the boonies?

00:08:13.952 --> 00:08:15.662
Huh?

00:08:24.880 --> 00:08:28.091
Where are we?

00:09:01.750 --> 00:09:03.544
The Otherside.

00:09:05.587 --> 00:09:07.714
Yep.

00:09:07.714 --> 00:09:11.510
Toriko, have you ever been here at night?

00:09:11.510 --> 00:09:16.390
No. Satsuki said it's too dangerous.

00:09:20.561 --> 00:09:23.021
Sorawo, did you bring your gun?

00:09:23.021 --> 00:09:24.940
Of course not.

00:09:24.940 --> 00:09:27.734
Who brings a gun to go out drinking?

00:09:27.734 --> 00:09:29.903
Wait, did you bring yours?!

00:09:31.071 --> 00:09:34.741
I was just thinking I wish I did.

00:09:34.741 --> 00:09:37.119
Me, too.

00:09:53.510 --> 00:09:55.262
How'd we end up on the Otherside?

00:09:55.262 --> 00:09:59.725
After we left the café, I thought
I saw everything flicker for an instant.

00:09:59.725 --> 00:10:03.854
Actually, things didn't seem
quite right even before that.

00:10:03.854 --> 00:10:07.566
Was that café an entrance to the Otherside?

00:10:07.566 --> 00:10:10.903
Why now, after we've been there so many times?

00:10:10.903 --> 00:10:14.573
It's not like we did anything
weird while we were--

00:10:14.573 --> 00:10:16.074
The hat?!

00:10:16.074 --> 00:10:17.284
That's it!

00:10:17.284 --> 00:10:20.162
I put on Lady Hasshaku's hat!

00:10:20.162 --> 00:10:22.789
I told you you shouldn't put that thing on!

00:10:22.789 --> 00:10:25.209
W-We don't know that's what caused it!

00:10:25.209 --> 00:10:28.128
You just said, "That's it!"

00:10:28.128 --> 00:10:30.964
I'd say it's a distinct possibility.

00:10:30.964 --> 00:10:35.052
Then maybe I should try it on again.

00:10:35.052 --> 00:10:38.472
No, no, don't! Don't even touch that thing!

00:10:38.472 --> 00:10:43.602
F-Fine, I won't touch it... okay?

00:10:43.602 --> 00:10:45.521
Okay.

00:10:46.730 --> 00:10:48.857
So, what now?

00:10:48.857 --> 00:10:55.364
We should stay put for now,
before we step on a glitch.

00:11:00.619 --> 00:11:01.537
Sorawo?

00:11:01.537 --> 00:11:03.163
Hm?

00:11:03.163 --> 00:11:06.041
I think we're about to have a change in plans.

00:11:06.041 --> 00:11:07.835
Huh?

00:11:21.265 --> 00:11:23.350
Are those...?

00:11:24.560 --> 00:11:26.311
It can't be.

00:11:27.896 --> 00:11:29.690
Are those bodies?

00:11:29.690 --> 00:11:31.859
No way...

00:11:34.736 --> 00:11:37.114
Sorawo? What is that?

00:11:37.114 --> 00:11:38.574
Let's not wait to find out!

00:11:38.574 --> 00:11:39.908
Run!

00:12:08.437 --> 00:12:11.857
Sorawo! Should we really be
running like this? What about glitches?

00:12:11.857 --> 00:12:15.777
Follow right behind me. Don't stray an inch!

00:12:33.170 --> 00:12:34.922
A hill!

00:12:36.590 --> 00:12:39.009
It's pretty steep.

00:12:41.929 --> 00:12:42.971
Toriko!

00:12:42.971 --> 00:12:46.099
I'm all right. I can make it.

00:13:12.167 --> 00:13:13.085
What is it?

00:13:13.085 --> 00:13:15.754
Don't stop! Go!

00:13:20.092 --> 00:13:21.051
Sorawo!

00:13:21.051 --> 00:13:22.886
Ow.

00:13:24.721 --> 00:13:26.348
Gravel?

00:13:26.348 --> 00:13:28.016
It's coming!

00:13:32.396 --> 00:13:32.855
--That way!

00:13:32.855 --> 00:13:34.523
--Huh?!
--That way!

00:13:36.066 --> 00:13:37.860
Did you see something?

00:13:37.860 --> 00:13:40.279
There might be a station.

00:13:43.824 --> 00:13:45.993
Huh? What's that?

00:13:48.078 --> 00:13:50.664
F-Faces?!

00:13:57.212 --> 00:13:58.714
Sorawo! Move!

00:13:58.714 --> 00:14:01.425
Don't give up! Come on!

00:14:16.356 --> 00:14:20.652
It'll work out as long as there's the two of us.

00:14:34.249 --> 00:14:35.375
What is it?

00:14:35.375 --> 00:14:37.753
Sorawo, this way!

00:14:37.753 --> 00:14:40.130
Get down.

00:14:40.130 --> 00:14:41.173
What is it?

00:14:41.173 --> 00:14:43.091
Keep your head down.

00:15:08.825 --> 00:15:10.327
Halt.

00:15:12.037 --> 00:15:13.622
Halt!

00:15:14.122 --> 00:15:15.666
Don't shoot!

00:15:15.666 --> 00:15:18.293
Don't shoot! Don't shoot!

00:15:21.588 --> 00:15:24.007
You're human?

00:15:24.007 --> 00:15:25.926
W-We're human.

00:15:25.926 --> 00:15:29.721
Hey, Lieutenant! That thing's still out there!

00:16:37.206 --> 00:16:39.041
Are you all right?

00:16:39.041 --> 00:16:41.877
Th-Thank you.

00:16:41.877 --> 00:16:42.961
They're human?

00:16:42.961 --> 00:16:45.047
Are they really human?

00:16:45.047 --> 00:16:47.299
They could be one of them.

00:16:47.299 --> 00:16:49.760
Lieutenant, stand back.

00:16:49.760 --> 00:16:53.597
They gotta be wild things. Let's get 'em!

00:17:01.522 --> 00:17:05.984
Stand down, Greg. You saw them
being chased by the Horned Man, too.

00:17:05.984 --> 00:17:07.444
They're human.

00:17:07.444 --> 00:17:08.820
But sir...

00:17:08.820 --> 00:17:11.532
This is an order, Master Sergeant.

00:17:11.532 --> 00:17:13.992
Lower your weapon.

00:17:16.245 --> 00:17:18.121
Damn.

00:17:18.121 --> 00:17:22.292
Who are you? Where did you come from?

00:17:22.292 --> 00:17:25.671
I-Ikebukuro... in Tokyo.

00:17:25.671 --> 00:17:26.171
--Tokyo?!

00:17:26.171 --> 00:17:27.214
--Tokyo?!
--Did she say Tokyo?

00:17:27.214 --> 00:17:30.509
That's hundreds of miles from here.

00:17:30.509 --> 00:17:32.553
Where'd you come from?

00:17:32.553 --> 00:17:33.846
Okinawa.

00:17:33.846 --> 00:17:35.013
Okinawa?!

00:17:35.013 --> 00:17:38.141
So then, you're U.S. forces stationed in Japan?

00:17:38.141 --> 00:17:39.893
We're marines.

00:17:39.893 --> 00:17:43.480
I'm the commander of Pale Horse
Battalion, Charlie Company 1/2,

00:17:43.480 --> 00:17:45.774
Lieutenant Will Drake.

00:17:50.153 --> 00:17:54.241
I take it you two don't know
how to get out of here, either.

00:17:54.241 --> 00:17:59.746
Y-Yeah. We don't even know how
we ended up on the Otherside.

00:17:59.746 --> 00:18:01.707
That's too bad.

00:18:01.707 --> 00:18:06.503
I thought we'd be able
to escape this living hell.

00:18:06.503 --> 00:18:12.551
I'm sorry, but I might not be able
to help you return to our world.

00:18:12.551 --> 00:18:18.849
We've been here on the Otherside for
over a month but have yet to find a way out.

00:18:18.849 --> 00:18:22.895
How did you get here?

00:18:22.895 --> 00:18:26.398
We were training in the mountains when...

00:18:30.444 --> 00:18:34.615
Our unit ended up here before we realized it.

00:18:34.615 --> 00:18:40.621
By the time we noticed the vegetation
differed from Okinawa, it was too late.

00:18:40.621 --> 00:18:47.044
We regrouped and set up a perimeter
with the station as our base,

00:18:47.044 --> 00:18:50.255
but we've suffered more than a few casualties.

00:18:51.215 --> 00:18:54.968
Casualties? Did that monster get them?

00:18:54.968 --> 00:18:57.137
Only a few of them.

00:18:57.137 --> 00:19:00.933
Did you see those bodies
hanging down from its belly?

00:19:00.933 --> 00:19:02.893
I-I did.

00:19:05.187 --> 00:19:09.316
They were our comrades. The mule was ours, too.

00:19:09.316 --> 00:19:13.946
The mule? You mean that thing that
looks like a giraffe without a neck?

00:19:13.946 --> 00:19:19.368
It was a robotic pack mule assigned to our unit.

00:19:19.368 --> 00:19:22.621
While carrying the bodies,
it stepped on a weird sort of bear trap

00:19:22.621 --> 00:19:24.706
and was unable to move.

00:19:24.706 --> 00:19:31.046
We were forced to abandon it there,
but it reappeared later as you saw it,

00:19:31.046 --> 00:19:34.299
and it started attacking us.

00:19:34.299 --> 00:19:38.178
A bear trap? Maybe it's a glitch.

00:19:38.178 --> 00:19:41.098
Was that sound from the motor?

00:19:41.098 --> 00:19:44.101
I can't believe machines are affected, too.

00:19:44.101 --> 00:19:46.937
You mentioned a station.

00:19:46.937 --> 00:19:52.192
Yes, Station February.
It's as small as it is old.

00:19:52.192 --> 00:19:55.779
February? Why's it named that?

00:19:55.779 --> 00:19:58.490
That's what was written there.

00:20:03.120 --> 00:20:04.746
The station!

00:20:31.315 --> 00:20:34.234
Where's the electricity coming from?

00:20:34.234 --> 00:20:35.777
I don't know.

00:20:35.777 --> 00:20:41.491
It was all lit up when we got here,
but I haven't seen any power lines.

00:20:41.491 --> 00:20:45.245
Are there any other abandoned stations?

00:20:45.245 --> 00:20:48.832
We haven't found any others yet.

00:20:48.832 --> 00:20:51.877
And this one doesn't appear to be abandoned.

00:20:51.877 --> 00:20:53.962
Huh? This is...

00:20:56.715 --> 00:20:59.718
"Kisaragi"
"Katasu - Yami"
Station February is...

00:21:00.802 --> 00:21:03.805
...Kisaragi Station?

00:21:05.015 --> 00:21:06.350
This way.

00:21:06.350 --> 00:21:10.229
I guess there's no time to see the sights.

00:21:57.985 --> 00:22:01.989
"Station February"

00:22:11.582 --> 00:22:15.836
<i>My hair was tossed by the cold wind</i>

00:22:15.836 --> 00:22:19.965
<i>Did you notice me shut the window?</i>

00:22:19.965 --> 00:22:24.261
<i>I lose my nerve when we get so close</i>

00:22:24.261 --> 00:22:28.140
<i>I don't need something that won't last</i>

00:22:28.140 --> 00:22:30.267
<i>Flashbacks hurt</i>

00:22:30.267 --> 00:22:31.894
<i>Ever-lingering shadows</i>

00:22:31.894 --> 00:22:36.064
<i>I know I'm too bound by the past, aren't I?</i>

00:22:36.064 --> 00:22:38.483
<i>Hey, this feeling we felt</i>

00:22:38.483 --> 00:22:44.072
<i>There's no doubt about it,</i>
<i>it's got to be special</i>

00:22:44.072 --> 00:22:47.910
<i>You and me, crisscrossing emotions</i>

00:22:47.910 --> 00:22:52.122
<i>I don't want to look back with regret</i>

00:22:52.122 --> 00:22:56.960
<i>I tell myself to believe</i>

00:22:56.960 --> 00:23:00.923
<i>And I tell my heart,</i>
<i>trust me, trust me, so sparkly</i>

00:23:00.923 --> 00:23:04.718
<i>It's the rhythm of a racing pulse</i>

00:23:04.718 --> 00:23:08.931
<i>As I gazed at your outstretched hand</i>

00:23:08.931 --> 00:23:15.062
<i>I decided I'd put my trust in you</i>

00:23:15.062 --> 00:23:23.529
<i>I will change myself, change myself</i>
<i>I will change myself, change myself</i>

00:23:23.529 --> 00:23:30.869
<i>I will change myself, change myself</i>
<i>I will</i>

00:23:32.496 --> 00:23:34.790
It appears they've gone missing.

00:23:34.790 --> 00:23:35.082
"Absent"                                "Absent"
It appears they've gone missing.

00:23:35.082 --> 00:23:38.293
"Absent"                                "Absent"
In their stead, I thought I'd
give a nearly one-hour lecture

00:23:38.293 --> 00:23:39.545
"Absent"                                "Absent"
on the mechanism by which
people experience fear.

00:23:39.545 --> 00:23:41.296
on the mechanism by which
people experience fear.

00:23:41.296 --> 00:23:42.923
What? A call from Sorawo and Toriko?

00:23:42.923 --> 00:23:43.215
"Absent"                                "Absent"
What? A call from Sorawo and Toriko?

00:23:43.215 --> 00:23:43.382
"Absent"                                "Absent"
--Error... trap. Probably safe.

00:23:43.382 --> 00:23:45.425
"Absent"                                "Absent"
--Error... trap. Probably safe.
--Speaking nonsense to oneself.

00:23:45.425 --> 00:23:47.072
"Absent"                                "Absent"
Hmph, just a crank call.
